        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for kind words!\r\n\r\nThe 'mini.completion' module [uses built-in tools as much as possible](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/061379f082d6b03305b00ddd6f8f6b7b8eded6d8/doc/mini-completion.txt#L13-L14). This includes the popup menu with completion candidates (see `:h ins-completion-menu`). Its maximum height can be controlled by 'pumheight' option. You can adjust it by putting something like `vim.o.pumheight = 10` in your Lua config. An alternative is to use 'mini.basics' and its [`options.extra_ui` setting](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/061379f082d6b03305b00ddd6f8f6b7b8eded6d8/doc/mini-basics.txt#L172) with something like this: `require('mini.basics').setup({ options = { extra_ui = true } })`.",
